ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO1", "As we enter the trial we will find a small add group right at the beginning which are easy to deal with. Once completed we will go around the cliff to the left and wait at the top of the ladder ready to deal with the first boss.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO2", "We eliminate the first mini boss in the middle on the platform. Then we have to activate the 2 fire bowls besides him for the first boss to spawn. The tank can have the boss remain in the large pool and face him away from the group who can space out behind him.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO3", "Popcorn Circles - Three red circles will be put on random players. The boss raises his staff & players will then get the popcorn with a green and then red circle slowly appearing underneath the player. The circle will stun you and then you will be thrown in the air. You have to dodge roll out of the first circle.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO4", "Culminating Slam - After the second round of the popcorn circles, the Mantikora will do a huge AoE damage. If possible, block it. Healers have to heal everyone to 100% after this, because players will get bleeding damage that only goes off when you get back to 100% HP.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO5", "Poison Shard Circles - The boss drops red circles with a green shard in it that deal a lot of poison damage. They will drop at the players standing the furthest from the boss. Block when the circle lands or it will stun and slow you and you will most likely die. Move out of it as soon as the shard lands, just walk out of it asap.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO6", "Feeding Pit Achievement - In the cave to the left of the first boss is a large piece of meat. A member of the group needs to collect this for use later in the trial to be able to gain the Feeding Pit Achievement.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO7", "Next up is a small group of mobs who wont do too much damage and are easy to kill.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO8", "The next add group is waiting for us before the bridge. All the following trash groups will have Overchargers, Rockheaver Trolls, Warpriests and smaller mobs in it. The main tank has to taunt the Trolls and the Warpriest whereas the off tank has to deal with the Archers and Overchargers. It is very important to kill Overchargers first.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO9", "Overchargers - They place lightning circles on random players that do a lot of damage. Use a shield like Harness Magicka. Players with lightning have to move out of the group then stand still. Small circles appear on the ground that will follow one player, stay out of them and the group, otherwise you will bring the circles into the group.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO10", "Poison - Snake columns & Trolls put a poison AoE. If you are to close to a player with poison it infects you. You will have a green aura and a red circle underneath you. It is important to stay away from other players and STAND STILL to not infect other players, because this poison does big damage.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO11", "On the bridge are Overchargers(target these first) & Trolls. Beware of the holes in the bridge. The tank can pull the Trolls and keeps then away from the group. Only go 3/4 of the way across the bridge as at the end of the bridge is the 2nd Boss that we don't want to attack yet. When the mobs are dead go back to the start of the bridge.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO12", "The tank has to go across the bridge and pull the Troll to the start of the bridge, the rest of the group has to stay at the start of the bridge. The position is key, if the tank pulls the Troll way too much towards the beginning of the bridge, he will reset. If he pulls him not enough towards it, the Overchargers will join the fight.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO13", "Three Way Avalanche - The Troll has a frontal Avalanche damage skill that flows away from him in three straight lines. The main tank has to focus on facing the Troll towards him, to avoid that this attack directs its damage into the group. If you see his Avalanche attack, just take a step aside, to avoid getting hit by it or block.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO14", "Stomp - From time to time, the Troll will stomp. This deals a lot damage in a round AoE around him. Avoid standing in it when he is doing his stomp. Especially important for melee damage dealers. Use a shield to protect yourself.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO15", "Stone Throw - As soon as the Trolls holds up his arms, he will throw stones at random players in the group. The main tank can easily see this animation and warn the group to shield up and / or block. If you block when it hits you or are shielded up, you should survive. If it hits you unexpected you may die.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO16", "After killing the 2nd Boss its time to deal with all the Overchargers that spawned during the fight and are now waiting for us at the end of the bridge. The best option here is to all focus 1 Overcharger at a time whilst keeping the Overchargers inside our group AoE's.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO17", "During the following hallways and rooms we have to avoid hugging and touching the huge snake pillars, because they will also spread the poison fields we are already used to from the Trolls. Activate the two levers at the door at the same time to leave the bridge hall behind us.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO18", "The next large room has 2 doors and 2 levers on the right and left side. The Tank goes right where he tanks all Adds until everyone else has killed the mobs on the left. Once we have killed the mobs on both sides we can switch the levers at the top on each room and proceed with the next trash group containing some more Trolls.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO19", "With the next mobs make sure we don't go too fast & deal with each mob group one by one. At the next small room there is another group of mobs with Overchargers & Trolls. When this group is dead, we can go for the right door then the left door. We repeat this twice more in the following rooms. Its then 1 more mob group before the next boss.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO20", "This boss has some friends that will join the fight and make it a harder battle. During the fight a Troll, Overcharger, War Priest, Archer & two Skirmishers will spawn regularly. If you kill them during the fight, they will respawn after about 15 seconds.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO21", "The Tank has to tank Ozara & the Overcharger at the door on the right of the room. The off tank has to tank the War Priest, the Troll and the Archer at the entrance to the room, with enough space to the rest of the group with the Archer arrow spray facing him. The Trolls should not bother us and will not respawn if we don't kill them.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO22", "Group formation is key. Healers stand on each side of the boss and the rest of the group has to position themselves in two half-circles around the boss. Melee DDs in the first row, Ranged DDs in the second row. We have to stick to these positions during the whole fight. Make sure there is enough space between all players.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO23", "Pin Bolts - As soon as the fight starts, after 5 to 10 seconds, Ozara will start to pin two random players around her to the ground with a lightning AoE and a bolt sticking out of them. The player on the right or on the left side of you is in charge of unpinning you, every time you get pinned. Use your Synergy button to unpin people fast.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO24", "After we finished Ozara, the door to the next room will open and Trolls will enter the room. The Tank has to pull the Trolls asap and move them away from the group. In the next room you will have to deal with the last big trash group.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO25", "Before heading up the stairs to the last boss its time to do the Feeding Pit Achievement, we go through the door to the right and stack everyone on the Feed Pile. The member that picked the meat up needs to place it down now and the fight will start. A lot of Trolls will appear that we need to nuke down to get the achievement.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO26", "The tank tanks the Serpent on the platform he appears on facing him north, away from the group. The off tank has to pull all Adds (Mantikoras and Lamias) into the groups AoE but keep them facing away from the group as best they can. Everyone else stacks together on the platform behind the Serpent.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO27", "Poison Phase - When the boss goes down under the ground and appears in the middle of the platform centre the poison phase is incoming. The group has to stack closely so the healers can heal through this phase. When this phase is over, the Serpent does a cleave attack, so stay back until the Tank has him facing away from the group again.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO28", "Magicka Bombs - When one player has the Magicka Bomb, his character will shimmer blue. You then have 15 seconds to lose as much magicka as possible or you will die and damage the group as the bomb scales to your magicker. If you manage to lose enough magicka, the blue light will go away and you will regain some extra magicka.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NSO29", "Last Poison Phase - When the HP from the boss is very low, at about 1-4% he will start doing a last poison phase with high damage. Healers have their ultimate ready and have enough Magicka to heal through this last phase. DDs focus on killing the boss. Keep healing and doing DPS when he is at 0% as this phase will go on a little longer!")

