ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA1", "We run through the first rooms and upstairs to find the first mobs, Fire Atronachs, that are easy to kill in our group AoE. As we continue on we will start getting hit by lightning. Go and stand in the yellow circle that appears, this will stop the damage. This tactic will be used later on. Once all the group is in the circle we can move on.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA2", "Ice Room - Beware of the moving little ice cyclones on the ground, they will freeze you for a short period. You can easily run around them but if you run into one it doesn’t matter that much, it does not deal any damage, you just need to use stamina to break free.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA3", "After the Ice Room wait for all team members to get together and open the door. Two big Frost Atronachs will engage us. The tank has to turn these away from the group, because they use a frontal cone attack that deals damage. Also, take care of their red circle AoE that can spike you.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA4", "Next is the Bannerman Group with some Chainspinners & Overcharges, these both put a round AoE under a random player which does a lot of damage. Those players need to get away from the other players to avoid splash damage from going into the group. Tanks have just to make sure they pull all the mobs into the AoE damage skills.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA5", "Lightning Storm Atronach - The Atronach awaits us on a big round platform. The tank can pull him on this platform, facing him towards the bridge and away from the group. The rest of the group just stacks behind the boss. Impending Storm - When the Atronach arches his back he will unleash a red AoE circle around him. You need to block this.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA6", "Lightning Strikes(Yellow Circles) - The sky goes a bit darker & lightning strikes hit, there will be a single yellow circle in the area around him. There are 5 possible spawn points of the yellow circles. We ALL have to stand in the yellow circle very quickly or we die.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA7", "Every team member has to stand on a platform, so that the beam-me up port to the next area is activated. Each group will be ported to the next area, where you will have to fight against an add group before you can regroup. The middle group crouch to avoid fighting until the 2 side groups have killed their mobs or the middle mobs will respawn.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA8", "Now reunited, a big group of Bannersman Adds will spawn. The group has to stack on the rock which you see in front of you, to make healers life easier. The tanks have to pull all the mobs that are out of range into your AoE damage. Kill Overchargers & Healers, then Chainspinners, then other Adds.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA9", "Big Quake - The boss will pound the ground when he stands up. It is a huge AoE and will last about 6 seconds; doing 5 ground pounds each time this mechanic comes up. When he stands up, the group must stack together on the healers in front of the boss so that they can heal the group through it.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA10", "Boulder Throw - This happens when he kneels down & the Boss' health falls below 80-75%. Boulders will then be thrown at random members and this attack will happen after each Big Quake attack. The group has to spread out and block. The boulders will do more damage and hit other members if we are grouped together as the damage stacks.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA11", "Two type of adds will spawn during this fight, Chainspinners throw an AoE attack (Fury Unleashed) on the ground and Nullifiers will shoot at random players. The off tank can pull them and they will burn down in the group AoE.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA12", "After we finished the Stone Atronach, it is time again to split into three groups again and use the platforms after the bridge on the top. The middle group can crouch to avoid combat until the 2 side groups have finished the same as before.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA13", "We will need to split our 8 DDs into groups of two DDs (so that’s 4 groups of 2). One group can also be made of the off tank and one healer, so that at the end, 5 groups of two players are available. Varlariel will split herself into her lookalike adds, you will have to burn those adds down as fast as possible.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA14", "Before the boss fights starts, we just have to make sure, every group of two players is covering one of the big pillars (except the mushroom pillar) around Varlariel and they know at which pillar they have to stand and once the add spawns kill the add at the right pillar and then kill any remaining adds, then go back to the boss.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA15", "Varlariel will constantly drop some small AoE circles on the ground during the whole fight. They will expand to a bigger circle after they hit the ground, so make sure you stand out of them. They also deal a lot of damage and if you stand in them and you are not shielding/ blocking, you can get oneshot.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA16", "She has an AoE Attack around her feet and in front of her, which hits really hard and is a one hit if you are not the tank. It is important that the tank begins the fight, make sure he always has the aggro from Varlariel. During the adds phase, he has to make sure no one is getting killed from the Frozen Breath attack.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA17", "During the first phase Varlariel will split herself into 3 Adds, in the second phase 4 Adds, in the third phase 5 Adds and after that she will split herself into 6 Adds. If you can’t kill the Adds fast enough, Varlariel will explode after about 20 seconds after the adds spawned and we will most likely wipe.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA18", "A number of adds will spawn and will need killing before the final boss will appear in the centre of the circle. This happens quickly so be ready to start the whole fight before starting the adds.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA19", "Chain Lightning - This attack from The Mage is applied to a random player. Anyone near that player will also take the splash damage. That is why we have to spread out around the mage. Make sure you keep enough space between you and the player next to you. Do not stack more than two players on one position.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA20", "Daedric Corruption Mines - The Mage will drop mines all around on her. They shine purple with a red circle around them. Avoid them if possible. You can disarm them by running through them. They will deal damage but if you shield yourself before you run over them, then it is possible to survive it.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA21", "Axes - The Mage will spawn conjured Axes, usually two at a time. The tanks have to taunt them on the rock at the start when they appear to get them away from the group. Tanks have to be in block all the time. Healers have to look after your tanks and support and heal them through the whole fight, throw them spears so they can recover stamina.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA22", "Conjured Reflection Adds (Mini Mages) - This Add will spawn past 50% HP of The Mage. The Add attacks with an AoE that consumes the life of random players. As soon as the Add spawns the DDs have to focus on her, because she has to be killed as soon as possible. If the add survives too long, it can wipe the group.")
ZO_CreateStringId("TTG_NAA23", "Once the Mage reaches 15% health, she will do 4 stage wide knockdowns, this will also kill the remaining adds and the Axes. The Mage will spam an intense AoE attack called the Arcane Vortex. Your healers have to use Solar Prison Ultimate and healing skills to keep your group alive. The damage gets stronger the longer the Mage lives.")

